    q("Which of the following is a function of a constitution?", ["To conduct elections", "To create the organs of government", "To collect taxes", "To appoint ambassadors"], 1, "A constitution creates the organs and distributes power between them. Elections, taxes and appointments are things the organs do once they exist."),
    q("A constitution that is contained in one document is said to be", ["written", "rigid", "flexible", "unwritten"], 0, "Written. Whether it is hard to amend is a separate test, so written and rigid are not synonyms."),
