    q("A constitution is rigid when it", ["is written down", "can be amended only by a special procedure", "cannot be amended at all", "is enforced by the courts"], 1, "Rigidity is about the amending procedure — a special majority, a referendum or the consent of the states. A written constitution can be flexible, and no constitution is literally unamendable."),
    q("The main disadvantage of a flexible constitution is that", ["it cannot be changed", "rights may be altered by a simple majority", "it requires a referendum for every change", "it cannot be written down"], 1, "Because ordinary legislation can change it, a temporary majority can alter fundamental rules. Its advantage is that it keeps pace with change."),
