    q("Which of the following is a residual matter?", ["Citizenship", "Police", "Chieftaincy", "Customs and excise"], 2, "Chieftaincy is not on the exclusive or concurrent list, so it is residual and only a state House of Assembly may legislate on it."),
    q("Where a state law conflicts with a federal law on a matter in the concurrent list", ["the state law prevails", "the federal law prevails", "both laws remain in force", "the Constitution is amended"], 1, "The federal law prevails, by the doctrine of covering the field, and the state law is void only to the extent of the inconsistency."),
    q("Federalism is best defined as a system in which", ["all power is held by the central government", "governmental power is divided between a central government and constituent units, each deriving its authority from the constitution", "the units may secede at will", "the central government may abolish the units"], 1, "The defining feature is constitutional division of power between levels, neither level being the creation of the other. A unitary system concentrates power, and a confederation is looser than a federation."),
