    q("The Aba Women's Riots of 1929 were a protest against", ["the imposition of direct taxation and warrant chiefs", "the creation of the regions", "the Clifford Constitution", "the deportation of a chief"], 0, "The riots followed the extension of direct taxation to the east and the resentment of the warrant chiefs the British had created where no chiefs existed."),
    q("Which of the following is NOT a reason for the rigidity of the Nigerian Constitution?", ["It protects fundamental rights", "It safeguards the federal structure", "It allows the President to amend it by decree", "It prevents hasty amendment"], 2, "The President cannot amend the Constitution by decree; section 9 requires the National Assembly and the states. Protection of rights, the federal structure and protection against haste are the reasons for rigidity."),
